But IMPORTANT: I would not blindly paste this into the repo yet.

There are two reasons.

First, some of the IDs/classes above are architectural names we've discussed, but your existing JS modules are the actual authority. We need to make sure terminal.js, book-education.js, blog-horizontal-scroll.js, logo.js, etc. are all getting exactly the elements they expect.

Second, your logo is missing from that skeleton deliberately. We know what you want visually, but logo.js already has a specific discovery mechanism. We should wire its actual expected element into the HTML rather than inventing one.

So the next move should be:

HTML DOM contract → compare against every JS module → fix IDs/classes → then write the actual index.html.

That gives us this pipeline:

